# ============================================================================
# ocrmd - environment template
# ============================================================================
#
# Copy this file to .env and uncomment what you use:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# NEVER commit .env to version control (.gitignore already ignores it).
#
# Where ocrmd looks: ./.env in the current directory, then the project root,
# then ~/.config/ocrmd/.env. The first file found wins, and it never overrides
# a variable already set in the environment.
#
# Everything here is optional. Without credentials ocrmd runs OCR-only, and
# `ocrmd verify` fills in the model pass later. Leave a line commented rather
# than empty: an empty value is still set in the environment, and not every
# reader treats it as missing.
# ============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model credentials (one is enough; docs/setup.md says which models each reaches)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anthropic Console API key: reaches every model, and `verify --batch` needs it.
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Claude Code / subscription OAuth token (`claude setup-token`), re-exported as
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN. The API serves only claude-haiku-5-5 to it, so also
# uncomment the OCRMD_MODEL line below.
#CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# Any other bearer token for the Anthropic API; same rules as the OAuth token.
#ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=
# xAI API key, for `--provider xai` (or provider = "xai" in ocrmd.toml).
#XAI_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ocrmd settings (any Settings field works as OCRMD_<FIELD>)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where all data lives (raw/, processed/, documents/, ocrmd.db, ...).
# Default: the project directory.
#OCRMD_ROOT=
# The transcription model. Default: claude-opus-5-5.
#OCRMD_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tools
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A headless Chrome for `ocrmd reconstruct` when it is not in a standard place.
#CHROME=
# Development only: `FLEET_ASSIST=1 ocrmd serve` adds the fleet's assistant panel to the web UI, so a Claude Code
# session paired through the Harness Console on this machine can see the page you have open. Off by default.
#FLEET_ASSIST=1

# Every other OCRMD_* variable, with its type and default, is in the generated
# settings reference: docs/reference/settings.md (OCRMD_SINKS takes JSON).
